          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "приводить (privodít) — \"to lead to, to result in\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Спешка часто приводит к ошибкам. Spéshka chásto privódit k oshíbkam. Haste often leads to mistakes."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Imperfective; present привожу, приводишь; perfective привести. Приводить к + dative — to lead to. It also means to bring someone along: привести друга."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "приводить (privodít) is built from при- \"to, towards\" and водить \"to lead\", from Proto-Slavic voditi \"to lead, to conduct\" (EtymDB). A cause leads to its result."
            }
          ]
        },
