            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "влиять (vliyát) — \"to influence, to affect\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Погода влияет на моё настроение. Pogóda vliyáyet na moyó nastroyéniye. The weather affects my mood."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Imperfective; perfective повлиять. Влиять на + accusative."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "влиять (vliyát) was taken from Church Slavonic vŭlĭjati (EtymDB) \"to pour in\", built from в- \"into\" and the root of лить \"to pour\". To influence someone was to pour something into them."
            }
          ]
        },
